data.content:
Your code **doesn't use `Thread.Abort`**, `Thread.Interrupt`, or catch `ThreadAbortException`. It only uses `Thread.Start`, `Thread.Join`, and `Thread.Sleep` — all of which work identically on .NET 8.

**This code requires no Thread.Abort migration.** It will compile and run as-is on .NET 8.

That said, for a modernization opportunity (unrelated to Thread.Abort), you could replace manual thread management with `Parallel.ForEach` or `Task.WhenAll`:

```csharp
public void RunBatch(List<WorkItem> items)
{
    Parallel.ForEach(items, item => Process(item));
}
```

This gives you thread pool efficiency and simpler code, but it's optional — your current code is already .NET 8 compatible.
